{"module":"housing-today","voice":"male","duration":174.0,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Housing today: evictions, screening and keeping homes","start":0.0,"end":4.28,"words":[[0.05,0.55],[0.55,1.05],[1.34,2.09],[2.38,2.96],[2.96,3.21],[3.21,3.63],[3.63,4.04]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Redlining and urban renewal are history (see “Place” and “Burned, flooded and taken”).","start":5.08,"end":11.3,"words":[[5.12,5.89],[5.89,6.14],[6.14,6.48],[6.48,7.08],[7.08,7.16],[7.16,7.76],[7.76,7.93],[7.93,8.35],[8.35,8.61],[8.61,9.03],[9.33,9.84],[9.84,10.09],[10.09,10.69]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This lesson is about what keeps families from stable homes now.","start":11.65,"end":16.0,"words":[[11.7,11.92],[11.92,12.3],[12.3,12.46],[12.46,12.84],[12.84,13.07],[13.07,13.37],[13.37,13.9],[13.9,14.21],[14.21,14.74],[14.74,15.12],[15.12,15.43]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Evictions","start":16.35,"end":17.43,"words":[[16.4,17.23]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Princeton's Eviction Lab has found that Black renters, especially Black women, face eviction filings far out of proportion to their share of renters.","start":18.13,"end":28.81,"words":[[18.17,18.95],[18.95,19.55],[19.55,19.81],[19.81,20.07],[20.07,20.5],[20.5,20.76],[20.76,21.1],[21.1,21.71],[22.01,22.7],[22.7,23.05],[23.05,23.56],[23.87,24.21],[24.21,24.82],[24.82,25.42],[25.42,25.59],[25.59,25.85],[25.85,26.03],[26.03,26.72],[26.72,26.89],[26.89,27.15],[27.15,27.41],[27.41,27.58],[27.58,28.18]]},{"el":"s0","text":"An eviction record makes it harder to rent again.","start":29.16,"end":32.27,"words":[[29.2,29.34],[29.34,29.84],[29.84,30.19],[30.19,30.55],[30.55,30.69],[30.69,30.97],[30.97,31.11],[31.11,31.4],[31.4,31.75]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 2017 New York City became the first city to guarantee tenants facing eviction a lawyer; several cities and states, including San Francisco, Washington, Maryland and Connecticut, have followed.","start":32.62,"end":47.73,"words":[[32.66,32.82],[32.82,33.95],[33.95,34.19],[34.19,34.43],[34.43,34.76],[34.76,35.24],[35.24,35.4],[35.4,35.72],[35.72,36.05],[36.05,36.21],[36.21,36.77],[36.77,37.33],[37.33,37.82],[37.82,38.38],[38.38,38.54],[38.54,38.95],[39.23,39.71],[39.71,40.11],[40.11,40.36],[40.36,40.92],[41.2,41.85],[41.85,42.09],[42.09,42.98],[43.26,43.98],[44.26,44.99],[44.99,45.23],[45.23,46.04],[46.32,46.56],[46.56,47.12]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Laws that punish calling 911","start":48.63,"end":51.78,"words":[[48.68,48.92],[48.92,49.17],[49.17,49.58],[49.58,49.99],[49.99,51.55]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Many cities adopted “nuisance” or “crime-free housing” ordinances that penalize landlords, and push them to evict tenants, after a certain number of police calls to a property.","start":52.48,"end":64.51,"words":[[52.53,52.87],[52.87,53.28],[53.28,53.86],[53.86,54.45],[54.45,54.53],[54.53,55.2],[55.2,55.7],[55.7,56.44],[56.44,56.69],[56.69,57.36],[57.36,58.11],[58.4,58.65],[58.65,58.9],[58.9,59.15],[59.15,59.31],[59.31,59.73],[59.73,60.4],[60.69,61.02],[61.02,61.19],[61.19,61.6],[61.6,62.02],[62.02,62.18],[62.18,62.6],[62.6,62.93],[62.93,63.1],[63.1,63.27],[63.27,63.93]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In Norristown, Pennsylvania, Lakisha Briggs was threatened with eviction after police were called during domestic violence attacks against her; she sued, the city repealed its ordinance and settled in 2014.","start":64.86,"end":78.04,"words":[[64.91,65.06],[65.06,65.78],[66.04,66.98],[67.24,67.67],[67.67,68.04],[68.04,68.26],[68.26,68.76],[68.76,68.98],[68.98,69.49],[69.49,69.78],[69.78,70.15],[70.15,70.29],[70.29,70.58],[70.58,71.09],[71.09,71.67],[71.67,72.25],[72.25,72.62],[72.62,73.05],[73.05,73.27],[73.53,73.67],[73.67,73.96],[74.22,74.36],[74.36,74.65],[74.65,75.09],[75.09,75.31],[75.31,75.82],[75.82,76.03],[76.03,76.47],[76.47,76.62],[76.62,77.49]]},{"el":"s1","text":"HUD warned in 2016 that such ordinances can violate fair housing law.","start":78.39,"end":83.79,"words":[[78.44,78.68],[78.68,79.0],[79.0,79.16],[79.16,80.2],[80.2,80.43],[80.43,80.75],[80.75,81.47],[81.47,81.71],[81.71,82.35],[82.35,82.59],[82.59,83.07],[83.07,83.31]]},{"el":"s1","text":"They are the mirror image of the CAREN problem: some people are punished for calling police, while others call police as a weapon.","start":84.14,"end":92.09,"words":[[84.19,84.42],[84.42,84.5],[84.5,84.66],[84.66,84.97],[84.97,85.36],[85.36,85.52],[85.52,85.67],[85.67,86.06],[86.06,86.69],[86.96,87.2],[87.2,87.59],[87.59,87.67],[87.67,88.14],[88.14,88.29],[88.29,88.68],[88.68,89.15],[89.43,89.74],[89.74,90.05],[90.05,90.29],[90.29,90.68],[90.68,90.83],[90.83,90.99],[90.99,91.46]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Screening by algorithm","start":92.99,"end":95.03,"words":[[93.04,93.72],[93.72,94.01],[94.01,94.88]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Landlords increasingly rely on tenant-screening scores.","start":95.73,"end":99.72,"words":[[95.78,96.41],[96.41,97.19],[97.19,97.58],[97.58,97.73],[97.73,98.75],[98.75,99.14]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 2024 SafeRent Solutions agreed to pay about $2.3 million to settle a Massachusetts lawsuit alleging its scores unfairly rejected Black and Hispanic applicants who used housing vouchers.","start":100.07,"end":115.02,"words":[[100.12,100.29],[100.29,101.49],[101.49,102.18],[102.18,102.87],[102.87,103.3],[103.3,103.47],[103.47,103.73],[103.73,104.16],[104.16,105.36],[105.36,105.88],[105.88,106.05],[106.05,106.48],[106.48,106.65],[106.65,107.6],[107.6,108.03],[108.03,108.63],[108.63,108.89],[108.89,109.23],[109.23,109.83],[109.83,110.61],[110.61,110.95],[110.95,111.21],[111.21,111.9],[111.9,112.67],[112.67,112.84],[112.84,113.19],[113.19,113.7],[113.7,114.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Many states and cities now ban rejecting applicants just because they use a voucher.","start":115.37,"end":120.94,"words":[[115.42,115.72],[115.72,116.16],[116.16,116.38],[116.38,116.75],[116.75,116.98],[116.98,117.2],[117.2,117.87],[117.87,118.53],[118.53,118.9],[118.9,119.28],[119.28,119.5],[119.5,119.72],[119.72,119.87],[119.87,120.39]]},{"el":"h3","text":"The ownership gap","start":121.84,"end":123.17,"words":[[121.88,122.05],[122.05,122.65],[122.65,122.9]]},{"el":"s3","text":"About 45% of Black households own their homes, compared with about 73% of non-Hispanic white households (Census Bureau).","start":123.87,"end":134.33,"words":[[123.92,124.32],[124.32,125.46],[125.46,125.62],[125.62,125.94],[125.94,126.75],[126.75,127.0],[127.0,127.24],[127.24,127.73],[128.01,128.58],[128.58,128.82],[128.82,129.23],[129.23,130.52],[130.52,130.69],[130.69,131.58],[131.58,131.9],[131.9,132.71],[132.71,133.2],[133.2,133.85]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Lower appraisals (see “Banking”), higher mortgage costs and less family wealth for down payments keep the gap wide.","start":134.68,"end":141.31,"words":[[134.73,135.02],[135.02,135.68],[135.68,135.82],[135.82,136.33],[136.59,136.88],[136.88,137.32],[137.32,137.68],[137.68,137.9],[137.9,138.12],[138.12,138.56],[138.56,138.85],[138.85,138.99],[138.99,139.29],[139.29,139.87],[139.87,140.09],[140.09,140.23],[140.23,140.45],[140.45,140.82]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In 2022 a federal task force (PAVE) issued an action plan on appraisal bias.","start":141.66,"end":147.91,"words":[[141.71,141.87],[141.87,142.98],[142.98,143.14],[143.14,143.7],[143.7,144.02],[144.02,144.26],[144.26,144.57],[144.85,145.17],[145.17,145.33],[145.33,145.73],[145.73,146.05],[146.05,146.21],[146.21,146.85],[146.85,147.32]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Keeping families housed","start":148.81,"end":150.56,"words":[[148.81,149.28],[149.28,149.93],[149.93,150.39]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Right to counsel in eviction court.","start":151.26,"end":153.31,"words":[[151.32,151.56],[151.56,151.68],[151.68,152.11],[152.11,152.23],[152.23,152.65],[152.65,152.9]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Repeal crime-free and nuisance ordinances that punish calls for help.","start":153.66,"end":158.61,"words":[[153.71,154.14],[154.14,154.83],[154.83,155.09],[155.09,155.69],[155.69,156.46],[156.46,156.72],[156.72,157.15],[157.15,157.5],[157.5,157.67],[157.67,158.1]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Source-of-income protections for voucher holders.","start":158.96,"end":161.92,"words":[[158.97,159.64],[159.64,160.3],[160.3,160.44],[160.44,160.84],[160.84,161.38]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Down-payment help and community land trusts that keep homes affordable for good.","start":162.27,"end":167.39,"words":[[162.32,163.13],[163.13,163.42],[163.42,163.64],[163.64,164.3],[164.3,164.6],[164.6,165.04],[165.04,165.26],[165.26,165.48],[165.48,165.85],[165.85,166.44],[166.44,166.58],[166.58,166.88]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Heirs' property help so families keep inherited homes and land (a pro bono quest).","start":167.74,"end":173.14,"words":[[167.78,167.99],[167.99,168.5],[168.5,168.79],[168.79,169.01],[169.01,169.52],[169.52,169.74],[169.74,170.39],[170.39,170.76],[170.76,170.97],[170.97,171.26],[171.26,171.41],[171.41,171.7],[171.7,172.14],[172.14,172.57]]}]}